          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Politics in Croton</strong><br>\nPythagoras and his followers became politically powerful in Croton. Their influence led to the establishment of a governance that reflected their ethical and philosophical values. However, this involvement in politics also led to tensions with other citizens, which would later have dire consequences for the Pythagorean community.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Downfall and the End of Pythagoras</strong><br>\nThe tension between the Pythagoreans and the ruling powers in Croton eventually led to the downfall of their community. Around 500 BC, the Pythagorean meeting places were attacked, and Pythagoras was forced to flee the city. His exact date and place of death are unknown, but it is believed he died a few years later.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Pythagoras</strong><br>\nDespite the mystery surrounding his life and the exact nature of his contributions, Pythagoras's influence endures. His ideas have permeated many fields, from mathematics to philosophy, and his legacy is a testament to the enduring power of intellectual curiosity and scholarly pursuit.</p>\n"
              },
